      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{58c62e995865713647a7115b|full_name}: No, bounding boxes for particle systems are automatically generated. See https://blogs.unity3d.com/2016/12/20/unitytips-particlesystem-performance-culling/ for more info. For some reason unity 2017 seems to calculate the location and size of the bounding box of a local particle system before the system gets moved by final IK.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-12-07T08:57:56.092Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I noticed that as of the engine update particle occlusion works differently. Say for example you've got some particles attached to your hand. If you hold your hand out in front of you, the particles will disappear. If you look towards where the particles are when your avatar is in T-Pose, the particles will re-appear. I'm guessing this has to do with the dynamic occlusion new to 2017. If at all possible please change the occlusion behavior of particle systems so the occlusion bounds are calculated after the IK moves them instead of before.",
  "error": null,
